.TH KITPRO-API 8 "September 2026" "KITPro Server" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
kitpro-api \- authenticated local KITPro Server control plane
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kitpro-api
.br
.B kitpro-api --version
.br
.B kitpro-server admin permissions USERNAME PERMISSION[,PERMISSION...] --confirm USERNAME
.br
.B kitpro-server admin service-scope USERNAME UNIT ACTION[,ACTION...] --confirm USERNAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kitpro-api
serves the loopback-only KITPro dashboard and communicates with the privileged
helper over its Unix socket. It is normally started by systemd as the
unprivileged kitpro-api account.
.PP
The root-only
.B admin permissions
command replaces a local administrator's Host Administration permissions and
revokes its active sessions. The root-only
.B admin service-scope
command replaces the exact systemd unit/action scopes for a restricted service
operator and also revokes active sessions. Permission changes are audited. The
final security administrator cannot be demoted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/kitpro-server
Package configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/kitpro-api/control.db
Control-plane SQLite database.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kitpro-helper (8)
